# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
apology-death.md:1: argue/readings: S2 is read 2 ways: apology-death.logic.r2 has "nothingness ∧ dreamless_best → gain_nothing"; apology-death.logic.r2.2 and apology-death.logic.r2.3 have nothing from it; they differ when only "death is a state of nothingness and utter unconsciousness, like a dreamless sleep" and "few days or nights of a life are passed better and more pleasantly than a night of sleep undisturbed even by dreams" are true, which the second allows
apology-death.md:1: argue/answered: S2: answered no, which keeps apology-death.logic.r2, to: Suppose "death is a state of nothingness and utter unconsciousness, like a dreamless sleep" and "few days or nights of a life are passed better and more pleasantly than a night of sleep undisturbed even by dreams" are true and "death, being nothingness, is an unspeakable gain" is false. Is S2, "Now if you suppose that there is no consciousness, but a sleep like the sleep of him who is undisturbed even by dreams, death will be an unspeakable gain.", true then?
apology-death.md:1: argue/readings: S4 is read 3 ways: apology-death.logic.r2 has "nothingness → eternity_one_night" and "eternity_one_night → gain_nothing"; apology-death.logic.r2.2 has "eternity_one_night" and "nothingness ∧ dreamless_best ∧ eternity_one_night → gain_nothing"; they differ when only "few days or nights of a life are passed better and more pleasantly than a night of sleep undisturbed even by dreams" is true, which the first allows; apology-death.logic.r2.3 has "nothingness → eternity_one_night" and "nothingness ∧ dreamless_best ∧ eternity_one_night → gain_nothing"
apology-death.md:1: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps apology-death.logic.r2.2, to: Suppose "few days or nights of a life are passed better and more pleasantly than a night of sleep undisturbed even by dreams" is true and "death is a state of nothingness and utter unconsciousness, like a dreamless sleep", "if death is nothingness, eternity is only a single night" and "death, being nothingness, is an unspeakable gain" are false. Is S4, "Now if death be of such a nature, I say that to die is gain; for eternity is then only a single night.", true then?
